.doc Strata showcase
.fontmarkers short
.h1 Showcase of Strata features [showcase]
This document uses what Strata can do in a page: a keycap such as {k:Ctrl-S}, an equation such as {eq:x^2+y^2=z^2} inside a line of text, a footnote{fn:A footnote is a marker that holds text; it is printed at the foot of the page.} and a reference to another section, {ref:figures}.
.h2 Keys and equations
Press {k:F12} to open the menu, then {k:Right} to choose Print.  The sum of the first n whole numbers is {eq:\frac{{n(n+1)}}{{2}}}, and Euler's identity is {eq:e^{{i\pi}}+1=0}.
.space 0.3
.h2 A picture and a table [figures]
.pic pictures/sample.png 3.0 A picture of 24 by 16 cells, drawn by a program.
.table 12 12 12
Marker | Shown as | Printed as
Keycap | a box | a rounded key
Footnote | [NOTE] | a note at the foot
Equation | an image | typeset TeX
.end
.pagebreak
.h2 The last page
This text is on a new page, because the page break above is a marker that starts one.  In a printout the section numbers and the footnote number are made when the pages are made.
